  "findings": [
    "Six cached files fully read and hash verified against pinned Git tree. CLI prints a constant message and package version; get_version returns the version string. Test CLI only asserts exit0 without inspecting output. No file enumeration, hashing, duplicate indexing or comparison implementation in inspected source. Reject-domain remains justified; remaining template/docs files not yet reviewed.",
    "Sixteen additional files fully read: package metadata declares Python3.8.1..<3.12 and no runtime dependencies; CLI entry point is the already-read version printer. Remaining source configuration is only about/version YAML and empty py.typed. Second test checks version dot count only. All tracked Python implementation/test files have now been read; no duplicate-search implementation found.",
    "Book usage/API pages are placeholders; example only installs package and prints version. Copier metadata identifies hyperfast-python-template skeleton. ReadTheDocs references docs/ paths although tracked documentation resides in book/. Notebook config allows execution errors. These are documentation/template observations, not executed build results; no installs or publishing performed.",
    "Fifteen additional tooling files fully read. CI declares Ubuntu/Python3.8 only; coverage80percent over the tiny version wrapper is not duplicate-search qualification. Workflow path triggers cover src/tests but not all dependency/config changes. No live CI outcomes inspected. Make lint excludes the separately defined mypy target.",
    "Makefile tests-cov-fail pipes pytest to tee without setting pipefail in its own recipe shell; outer workflow pipefail does not automatically establish the child Make shell behavior. Thus coverage/test failure propagation is not established by the recipe. Release jobs are separate from lint/test, with no explicit dependency gate in these workflow files. No make/install/release/cleanup commands were executed."
  ],
